ing, fluid, and acid–base issues"}, {"id": "03512239-4662-4e4f-9968-47ffd326749b", "type": "concept", "title": "Catheter infection/thrombosis context, hepatobiliary complications, bone disease, and micronutrient imbalance"}, {"id": "427e8253-dc83-4a2b-9eac-f4925e9ec061", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycling, oral/enteral transition, safe handoff, home infusion, and quality-of-life outcomes"}]}]}, {"id": "129c9c42-c453-4c52-9741-fe8be22627cf", "type": "topic", "title": "Oncology and Hematopoietic Cell Therapy", "description": "Cancer nutrition care integrates disease site, treatment toxicities, malnutrition/cachexia, survivorship, and goals of care without promoting unproven cures.", "children": [{"id": "1c506029-83e9-4778-9779-06e37fd276ca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Assessment and treatment toxicities", "description": "Students anticipate how therapy and tumor location affect intake and metabolism.", "children": [{"id": "76d5c965-3880-43a8-99fb-566eaef7180a", "type": "concept", "title": "Surgery, radiation, chemotherapy, immunotherapy, transplant, and treatment timeline"}, {"id": "256bbaaa-3060-43c2-bb25-ff294e524f59", "type": "concept", "title": "Mucositis, xerostomia, dysgeusia, nausea, diarrhea, constipation, dysphagia, malabsorption, and fatigue"}, {"id": "0b232d2a-c2ab-4e5d-a7d4-b3fa8750b2ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Weight/muscle trajectory, function, inflammation, food safety, and distress"}]}, {"id": "0134e70d-d8fd-40bd-b970-1ae73546e842", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intervention and nutrition support", "description": "Students select proportionate strategies aligned with treatment and goals.", "children": [{"id": "710c7923-e5ef-4316-aa55-19ee5293719e", "type": "concept", "title": "Symptom-adapted meals, energy/protein density, oral supplements, hydration, and micronutrient safety"}, {"id": "b12038c8-e59e-42f6-9684-55ce339cb350", "type": "concept", "title": "Enteral/PN indications, head-and-neck access planning, GI obstruction, and ethical tradeoffs"}, {"id": "f6be57a9-dc2f-430b-88c7-0e248b9b9a54", "type": "concept", "title": "Cachexia mechanisms, exercise/rehabilitation context, pharmacologic coordination, and evidence limits"}]}, {"id": "400cdd85-1b75-4f72-b7a8-e1d8d6dcf97d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Survivorship and palliative care", "description": "Students shift outcomes as treatment intent and patient priorities change.", "children": [{"id": "11dfaa22-a8e5-44bb-a64a-4990c8249e79", "type": "concept", "title": "Late effects, bone and cardiometabolic health, recurrence claims, and supplement interactions"}, {"id": "08f2955e-d5ba-482c-af1a-5f15a9156ad7", "type": "concept", "title": "Comfort feeding, appetite, dry mouth, nausea, bowel symptoms, family distress, and cultural meanings"}, {"id": "313c2a11-0b7e-4a00-a16f-f282809250d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Shared decisions, artificial nutrition/hydration benefits and burdens, time-limited trials, and hospice collaboration"}]}]}, {"id": "68294ec1-a18a-47d1-b77f-3c93cd914780", "type": "topic", "title": "Liver, Pancreatic, and Intestinal Failure", "description": "Advanced GI disease can create severe maldigestion, malabsorption, fluid loss, encephalopathy, and dependence on specialized nutrition support.", "children": [{"id": "d0b2e3ae-4e14-4010-9ef4-7c1d9f3f36f5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Advanced liver disease", "description": "Students interpret malnutrition amid ascites, edema, inflammation, and altered metabolism.", "children": [{"id": "19c36c75-6c0b-4e4e-a53f-11339203ef25", "type": "concept", "title": "Cirrhosis, portal hypertension, ascites, encephalopathy, sarcopenia, and transplant pathway"}, {"id": "301763dc-32f9-4ab3-a181-01279364cf20", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy/protein adequacy, meal timing, sodium/fluid context, micronutrients, and alcohol-related disease"}, {"id": "74c97c8f-b471-4c8f-9ffb-c50be10beb78", "type": "concept", "title": "Dry weight estimation, diuretics/lactulose interactions, late-evening intake, and monitoring"}]}, {"id": "9606007a-b2b8-4c4e-908e-0607bd290518", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pancreatic and malabsorptive disease", "description": "Students link anatomy and digestive failure to symptoms and deficiencies.", "children": [{"id": "418a3358-bc9c-4af6-bb34-1d826adfdc71", "type": "concept", "title": "Acute/chronic pancreatitis, exocrine insufficiency, cystic fibrosis context, and enzyme therapy"}, {"id": "9b38faf3-caf3-4639-8077-76edbcc5069d", "type": "concept", "title": "Fat malabsorption, fat-soluble vitamins, diabetes, pain, alcohol/tobacco, and meal pattern"}, {"id": "e3e6ab97-dedb-44c7-a0f2-38e519aeebbf", "type": "concept", "title": "Enzyme timing/dose context, adequacy, symptom response, and referral"}]}, {"id": "80befa19-cd98-4eb9-9136-a0a7aced9b1c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Short bowel and intestinal failure", "description": "Students use remaining anatomy and output to guide hydration and support decisions.", "children": [{"id": "f4ad76b9-fcc1-4a13-81df-66dce0e8a1af", "type": "concept", "title": "Resection anatomy, colon-in-continuity, adaptation, high-output stoma, and fistula"}, {"id": "21178fac-37d7-4e34-a3ef-3f4c8f8fcd46", "type": "concept", "title": "Oral rehydration concepts, sodium/magnesium, kidney stones, micronutrients, and diet pattern"}, {"id": "19ea22e4-279c-47dd-8fe4-f0dc22c69a15", "type": "concept", "title": "Enteral stimulation, PN/home support, medications, rehabilitation, and transition"}]}]}, {"id": "ef422f75-065a-4f1b-8d78-191d181909fa", "type": "topic", "title": "Advanced Kidney Disease and Renal Replacement Therapy", "description": "Advanced renal MNT integrates dialysis modality, residual function, catabolism, fluid, electrolytes, bone-mineral disease, diabetes, and treatment burden.", "children": [{"id": "dac882b5-9591-4055-9de2-08bafb389215", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Advanced CKD and kidney failure", "description": "Students balance preservation, adequacy, symptom relief, and preparation for replacement therapy.", "child