ecy, or harm.", "children": [{"id": "105c1d97-486a-448e-82a2-d3c5f13a811d", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, confidentiality, level-of-care decisions, involuntary treatment context, and boundaries"}, {"id": "421a59bc-0736-4fcd-9763-19bd1e14d04e", "type": "concept", "title": "Weight stigma, higher-weight eating disorders, LGBTQ+ populations, athletes, disability, and cultural foodways"}, {"id": "bcc9f415-477a-4e8e-8649-c170a1843cec", "type": "concept", "title": "Social media, supplements, diabetes technology manipulation, relapse planning, and referral"}]}]}, {"id": "56e063b5-f0c9-4e69-baf0-f34360f36510", "type": "topic", "title": "Pediatric Clinical Nutrition", "description": "Pediatric MNT protects growth and development while accounting for gestational age, feeding skill, caregiver capacity, disease, and family context.", "children": [{"id": "547c2117-77c3-44e6-9400-7a0ac3ff715d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Growth and assessment", "description": "Students interpret trajectories, not isolated percentiles.", "children": [{"id": "3d7ef4c8-5ead-488f-836a-e1b689b36edf", "type": "concept", "title": "Corrected age, growth charts, weight/length/BMI-for-age, velocity, and genetic potential"}, {"id": "22ad8f21-e073-4b58-b641-148e555ecbd3", "type": "concept", "title": "Gestational/birth history, feeding development, intake, GI symptoms, medications, and family food security"}, {"id": "9f6a5b79-f6a9-4bbc-b71d-4bf2089f2a2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Pediatric malnutrition indicators, body composition limits, labs, and developmental context"}]}, {"id": "10db7d3c-b8b7-481d-a033-361f59337f6c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Infant and child nutrition support", "description": "Students adapt enteral/PN principles to age, size, fluid limits, and growth.", "children": [{"id": "e8dbe8f8-f802-4d44-9ca3-9ef544882dcd", "type": "concept", "title": "Human milk, formula concentration, fortification, modulars, osmolality context, and micronutrients"}, {"id": "63218bb0-2068-4ba8-a